  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow much did Greta spend on the dozen brownies she made for herself? Greta made two dozen cream cheese swirl brownies for herself. The bakery charges $2.50 for each brownie Greta made for herself.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Greta made **two dozen** brownies:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 12 = 24 \\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nAt \\$2.50 per brownie:\n\n\\[\n24 \\times \\$2.50 = \\$60.00\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$60.00}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Greta made one dozen cream cheese swirl brownies for herself.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "One dozen is 12 brownies.\n\n\\[\n12 \\times \\$2.50 = \\$30.00\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$30.00}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many brownies did Greta package if she put four brownies in each box and filled three boxes? Additionally, here are some details: Greta labeled each of the three boxes with a different color sticker. The boxes were placed on a shelf beside the party decorations.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Greta packaged:\n\n\\[\n4 \\text{ brownies per box} \\times 3 \\text{ boxes} = 12 \\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\text{ brownies}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Greta's office party sent her home with three-quarters dozen brownies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Three-quarters of a dozen is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{4}\\times 12=9\n\\]\n\nSo, Greta’s office party sent her home with \\(\\boxed{9\\text{ brownies}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many individual brownies did Greta have left over from the entire day? One more thing you should know: Greta's friends had 4 dozen brownies waiting at her surprise party.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Convert the dozens to individual brownies:\n\n- Greta made: \\(1\\) dozen \\(=12\\)\n- She received from the office party: \\(\\frac34\\) dozen \\(=9\\)\n- Her friends had: \\(4\\) dozen \\(=48\\)\n\nAdding them:\n\n\\[\n12+9+48=69\n\\]\n\nSo, assuming none were eaten or otherwise used, Greta had \\(\\boxed{69\\text{ brownies}}\\) in total.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — During the surprise party, 1 1/2 dozen brownies were eaten.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "\\(1\\frac{1}{2}\\) dozen equals:\n\n\\[\n1.5 \\times 12 = 18 \\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the 18 eaten from the previous total of 69:\n\n\\[\n69-18=51\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{51\\text{ brownies}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Greta's office party sent her home with half a dozen brownies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Half a dozen is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}\\times 12=6\\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nRecalculating:\n\n\\[\n12+6+48-18=48\n\\]\n\nGreta had \\(\\boxed{48\\text{ brownies}}\\) left over.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
